        {
          "type": "note",
          "tone": "warning",
          "title": "Gotchas",
          "text": "- Le + moment of the day means every time: Le matin, je me lève à sept heures (every morning). Ce matin or demain matin point to one day. Likewise le samedi = every Saturday, while samedi = this coming Saturday.\n- Un jour = a day on the calendar; une journée = the day as time that passes. Same for un matin / une matinée and un soir / une soirée.\n- Faire la vaisselle, faire le ménage, faire la lessive, faire les courses: faire plus the article is fixed (“do the dishes”, “do the shopping”).\n- Le petit déjeuner, le déjeuner, le dîner. In Belgium, Switzerland and Quebec, dîner means lunch and souper means dinner.\n- Du lundi au vendredi = from Monday to Friday. Le week-end is masculine and singular: le week-end est long."
        },
