    {
      "id": "dormir-finir",
      "title": "Dormir et finir",
      "minutes": 6,
      "lede": "Two new groups of -ir verbs. Dormir loses a consonant in the singular, finir adds -iss- in the plural.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "title": "Dormir et finir",
          "headers": [
            "Sujet",
            "dormir",
            "finir"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "je",
              "dors",
              "finis"
            ],
            [
              "tu",
              "dors",
              "finis"
            ],
            [
              "il / elle",
              "dort",
              "finit"
            ],
            [
              "nous",
              "dormons",
              "finissons"
            ],
            [
              "vous",
              "dormez",
              "finissez"
            ],
            [
              "ils / elles",
              "dorment",
              "finissent"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "tone": "warning",
          "title": "Gotchas",
          "text": "- Dormir type: the singular drops the m: je dors, tu dors, il dort. Same pattern for sortir (je sors, nous sortons) and partir (je pars, nous partons). Not “je dorme”.\n- Finir type: -is, -is, -it, then -issons, -issez, -issent. Other verbs like it: choisir, réussir.\n- Spoken, il dort and ils dorment differ only by the m (dɔr / dɔrm), while il finit and ils finissent are easy to hear: fini / finis. Remember the -ent ending is silent.\n- Dormir and finir are verbs, not reflexive: je dors, not “je me dors”."
        },
        {
          "type": "phrases",
          "title": "Écoutez",
          "items": [
            {
              "fr": "Je dors huit heures par nuit."
            },
            {
              "fr": "Tu dors bien ?"
            },
            {
